  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>alfaxalone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>N01AX05</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Goodchild CS et al. 2020</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy male volunteers</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>alfaxalone</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_alfaxalone/Alfaxalone_Goodchild2020_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL</td><td>1.08</td><td>L/min</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>central volume of distribution (V1)</td><td>0.99</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>intercompartment CLs (Q2)</td><td>0.87</td><td>L/min</td><td><small>Q2</small></td></tr><tr><td>Q3</td><td>0.46</td><td>L/min</td><td><small>Q3</small></td></tr><tr><td>peripheral volumes of distribution (V2)</td><td>6.36</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>V3</td><td>19.1</td><td>L</td><td><small>V3</small></td></tr><tr><td>time to a BIS 50</td><td>0.94</td><td>minutes</td><td><small>tmax</small></td></tr></table><h4>About alfaxalone</h4><p>Alfaxalone is a steroid-based general anesthetic used to induce and maintain anesthesia. It is approved for veterinary use, where it is widely used as an anesthetic in animals, while in humans it is considered experimental.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3611058\">Wikidata Q3611058</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Alfaxalone\">Alfaxalone</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Goodchild CS et al. (2020). Pharmacokinetic and Pharmacodynamic Analysis of Alfaxalone Administered as a Bolus Intravenous Injection of Phaxan in a Phase 1 Randomized Trial. <i>Anesthesia and analgesia 130(3):704–714</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1213/ANE.0000000000004204\">10.1213/ANE.0000000000004204</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31124836\">31124836</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Goodchild_2020: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
